<!-- ===================== CONTENT ===================== -->

<SubSection title="Metal Casting" id="Metal Casting">
<p><strong>Metal casting</strong> is a manufacturing process where molten metal is poured into a mold cavity that represents the negative shape of a desired part.</p>

<Itemize>
<Item><strong>Pattern:</strong> Replica of final part (slightly oversized for shrinkage).</Item>
<Item><strong>Mold:</strong> Hollow cavity that metal is poured into.</Item>
<Item><strong>Core:</strong> Insert forming internal cavities.</Item>
<Item><strong>Riser:</strong> Reservoir feeding metal during solidification.</Item>
</Itemize>
</SubSection>

<!-- ===================== MOLD FILLING ===================== -->

<SubSubSection title="Mold Filling" id="Mold Filling">
<p>Laminar flow is preferred to prevent oxidation from turbulence.</p>

<Itemize>
<Item>Bottom-up filling</Item>
<Item>Low viscosity (<InlineEquation equation="\\mu" />)</Item>
<Item>Low filling velocity</Item>
<Item>Short flow length</Item>
</Itemize>
</SubSubSection>

<!-- ===================== SOLIDIFICATION ===================== -->

<SubSubSection title="Solidification" id="Solidification">
<p>As metal cools, it contracts and eventually solidifies.</p>

<p><strong>Shrinkage Allowance:</strong></p>

<DisplayEquation equation="L_{\\text{pattern}} = L_{\\text{final}}(1 + s)" />

<p>where <InlineEquation equation="s" /> is the alloy shrinkage fraction.</p>
</SubSubSection>

<!-- ===================== SHRINKAGE EXAMPLE ===================== -->

<SubSubSubSection title="Example Problem: Shrinkage Allowance" id="Example Problem: Shrinkage Allowance">

<p><strong>How long should the pattern be for a 100 mm aluminum casting?</strong></p>

<p>Given:</p>

<DisplayEquation equation="s = 0.013" />

<DisplayEquation equation="L_{\\text{pattern}} = 100(1.013) = 101.3\\ \\text{mm}" />

<p><strong>The pattern must be oversized by 1.3%.</strong></p>

</SubSubSubSection>

